// CI's signing of the Mac test host, and nothing else's (architecture review 2026-11,
// mac-platform#1, testing-ci-release#3). Only `Scripts/run-tests.sh --ci-mac-host` passes it,
// through xcodebuild's -xcconfig, so no setting in the project changes. It lives beside the
// script and not under esc-chatmail/Configuration/: that folder is a filesystem-synchronized
// group, and a file there that project.pbxproj's membershipExceptions do not name is copied
// into every product, so the shipped MushMail.app would have carried this file in its
// Resources (PR 498 review). Nothing reads it but -xcconfig <path>; the host that runs
// on a developer Mac is still signed with the team, and shares the installed MushMail's
// container and keychain group as before.
//
// A team-signed Mac build needs the team's development profile, because the Mac entitlements'
// keychain-access-groups must be backed by one, and CI has no profile. An unsigned build
// (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO) carries no entitlements at all, so its host is unsandboxed, and
// verify-mac-test-host.sh and MacUnitTestHostGuard refuse it, rightly: unsandboxed, the app's
// cleanup deletes the user's real ~/Documents/Messages. This signs ad hoc instead. The
// signature carries the entitlements the project's ENABLE_* settings generate (the App
// Sandbox among them) and the file below, which has no keychain-access-groups, so the sandbox
// is kept and no profile is needed, and both checks admit the host unchanged.
//
// The bundle ID gets a .ci suffix, so the host's container is
// ~/Library/Containers/com.esc.inboxchat.ci: on a developer Mac too, this host never opens the
// installed MushMail's container. Without a keychain access group the data protection keychain
// refuses the host's items (errSecMissingEntitlement, -34018), so the switch also skips
// KeychainServiceTests, the one Mac-plan suite that writes the real keychain; every other suite
// injects its keychain. Do not make KeychainService tolerate that error (a file-keychain
// fallback, dropping kSecUseDataProtectionKeychain, an XCTSkip on -34018): each would hide the
// bug where a signed-in session is gone after a relaunch (docs/mac-app-plan.md, PR C) in the
// signed local run.
//
// The entitlements file is set for the app alone: a build setting cannot be scoped to a target
// from here, so the setting is spelled through the product's name, which leaves the test
// bundle's empty (the test bundle has no entitlements in the project either).
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER =
ESC_CI_MAC_HOST_ENTITLEMENTS_MushMail = esc-chatmail/Resources/esc_chatmail-macOS-CI.entitlements
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS[sdk=macosx*] = $(ESC_CI_MAC_HOST_ENTITLEMENTS_$(PRODUCT_NAME))
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = $(inherited).ci
